#: src/getting-started.md:3
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed is an open-source code editor with built-in collaboration and AI tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started.md:7
msgid ""
"This guide covers the essential commands, environment setup, and navigation "
"basics."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started.md:9
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started.md:11
msgid "Welcome Page"
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started.md:13
msgid ""
"When you open Zed without a folder, you see the welcome page in the main "
"editor area. The welcome page offers quick actions to open a folder, clone a "
"repository, or view documentation. Once you open a folder or file, the "
"welcome page disappears. If you split the editor into multiple panes, the "
"welcome page appears only in the center pane when empty—other panes show a "
"standard empty state."
msgstr ""

#: src/getting-started.md:15
msgid ""
"To reopen the welcome page, close all items in the center pane or use the "
"command palette to search for \"Welcome\"."
msgstr ""

